<article class="env-corollary" id="0582">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0582">Corollary <span data-tag="0582">4.7.7.23</span>.</a> Let $n$ be an integer and let $F_0: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $F_1: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1 \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be functors of $n$-categories. Then the oriented fiber product $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \vec{\times }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1$ and the homotopy fiber product $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \times ^{\mathrm{h}}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1$ are also $n$-categories. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      By definition, the oriented fiber product $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \vec{\times }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1$ can be realized as an iterated fiber product 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \times _{ \operatorname{Fun}( \{ 0\} , \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) } \operatorname{Fun}( \Delta ^1, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \times _{ \operatorname{Fun}( \{ 1\} , \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) } \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1, \]
</div>
<p>
       which is an $n$-category by virtue of Propositions <a data-tag="0581" href="/tag/0581">4.7.7.22</a> and Remark <a data-tag="057X" href="/tag/057X">4.7.7.19</a>. The homotopy fiber product $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \times ^{\mathrm{h}}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1$ is a full subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \vec{\times }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1$, which coincides with $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \vec{\times }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_1$ for $n \leq -1$. Applying Remark <a data-tag="057V" href="/tag/057V">4.7.7.17</a>, we see that it is also an $n$-category. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></article>
